  "body": "What happens: `fanuc.cps` and `haas.cps` take the modal plane back to G17 only before the next XY arc, before a canned cycle and at section end (`restorePlane`). A COMP engage (`G41`/`G42` on the next G01) that follows an XZ (G18) or YZ (G19) arc is written while G18/G19 is still modal, so the control compensates in that plane, not in XY where every mill generator compensates.\n\nEvidence: found while writing the #374 probe stream (`crates/app/tests/inverted_support/mod.rs`). Before an XY arc was added between the G19 arc and the COMP record, the posted Fanuc program read `G19 G02 ... J-5 K0` then `G01 G42 X-25 Y10 Z-1 D01 F600` with no G17 between them. The fixture now inserts an XY arc to stay clear of this.\n\nExpected: the comp engage block (and the cancel) state G17 when the modal plane is not 17, or the post refuses by name.\n\nDone means: both scripts write G17 before a G41/G42/G40 block whenever the plane is not 17. A conformance test pins it: XZ arc, then COMP LEFT, then the lead.\n",
